    "summary": "Epic Alligator‑Other One jam with soaring Attics and tight grooves",
    "blurb": "The early show bursts out of the gate with a fiery Alligator→The Other One sequence that segues into an electric Attics Of My Life. Highlights include a scorching Good Lovin’ > China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider medley and a tight, propulsive rhythm section throughout.",
    "review": "Port Chester’s Capitol Theatre on June 24‑1970 delivered one of the most exhilarating early‑Dead outings. The band launched with a blistering Alligator → The Other One → Attics Of My Life sandwich that set the night ablaze, then kept the momentum rolling through a seamless Good Lovin’ > China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider stretch and a raucous Cosmic Charlie finish. Jerry’s guitar was described as “smoking” and “blazing,” soaring over Phil’s deep‑note bass lines while Bill Kreutzmann drove the jams with a powerful, propulsive feel. Bob Weir added his trademark outlaw‑cowboy vocal flair on Me & My Uncle and laid down gritty rhythm chops throughout. The crowd energy is captured vividly on the best audience tape, giving listeners both crystal‑clear ambience and enough fidelity to hear every nuance of this historic performance.",
